 36SI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2023Lu07:                          
 36SI2c  Phys Rev C 108, 014329 (2023)                                          
 36SI c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), August 08, 2023.                      
 36SI c  2023Lu07: experiments to study decays of {+36}Al and {+36}Mg were      
 36SI2c  carried out at NSCL-MSU, and at FRIB-MSU facilities. At the NSCL-MSU,  
 36SI3c  {+36}Al activity was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X),E({+48}Ca)=140      
 36SI4c  MeV/nucleon, followed by separation of fragments using A1900 fragment  
 36SI5c  separator. Mixed radioactive beam centered around {+33}Na was          
 36SI6c  delivered to the NSCL |b-decay counting station, where two Si PIN      
 36SI7c  detectors and a scintillator provided the information about the        
 36SI8c  energy loss (|DE) and time-of-flight (tof) for particle identification 
 36SI9c  of the ions. The separated ions were implanted in a CeBr{-3}           
 36SIAc  scintillator detector which was coupled to a position-sensitive        
 36SIBc  photomultiplier tube (PSPMT), and surrounded by the 16 segmented       
 36SICc  SeGa array of Ge detectors, and 15 LaBr3 detectors. At the FRIB-MSU,   
 36SIDc  {+36}Al activity was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,x),E({+48}Ca)=172.3    
 36SIEc  MeV/nucleon, followed by separation of fragments using the Advanced    
 36SIFc  Rare Isotope Separator (ARIS) separator. Mixed radioactive beam        
 36SIGc  centered around {+42}Si was delivered to the FRIB Decay Station        
 36SIHc  Initiator (FDSi), where two Si PIN detectors and a fast scintillator   
 36SIIc  provided the information about the energy loss (|DE) and time-of-flight
 36SIJc  (tof) for particle identification of the ions. The separated ions      
 36SIKc  were implanted in a YSO scintillator detector which was flanked by two 
 36SILc  scintillator veto detectors immediately upstream and downstream,       
 36SIMc  and surrounded by 11 HPGe clover detectors and 15 fast-timing LaBr{-3} 
 36SINc  detectors on one side and the neutron detector array VANDLE on the     
 36SIOc  other side. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, half-lives of the 
 36SIPc  decays of {+36}Mg g.s., {+36}Al g.s. and a newly-discovered isomer.    
 36SIQc  Theoretical calculations of levels, J|p and configurations of {+36}Al  
 36SIRc  and {+36}Si using FSU shell-model Hamiltonians with the CoSMo code.    
